{
  "title": "73: al-Muzzammil المزمل",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الْمُزَّمِّلُۙ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL MUZZAMMELO.\nO you wrapped up in your mantle!\nقُمِ الَّيْلَ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(2)\nQOMIL LAYLA ILLAA QALEELAN.\nStand vigil through the night, except for a little [of it],\nنِّصْفَهٗۤ اَوِ انْقُصْ مِنْهُ قَلِيْلًا ۙ‏(3)\nNISFAHU AWIN QUS MINHO QALEELAA.\na half, or reduce a little from that\nاَوْ زِدْ عَلَيْهِ وَرَتِّلِ الْقُرْاٰنَ تَرْتِيْلًا ؕ‏(4)\nAW ZID A’LAYHE WA RATTELIL QUR-AANA TARTEELAA.\nor add to it, and recite the Quran in a measured tone.\nاِنَّا سَنُلْقِىْ عَلَيْكَ قَوْلًا ثَقِيْلًا‏(5)\nINNAA SANULQEE A'LAYKA QAWLAN SAQEELAA.\nIndeed soon We shall cast on you a weighty discourse.\nاِنَّ نَاشِئَةَ الَّيْلِ هِىَ اَشَدُّ وَطْاً وَّاَقْوَمُ قِيْلًا ؕ‏(6)\nINNAA NAASHE-ATAL LAYLE HEYA ASHADDO WAT-ANW WA AQWAMO QEELAA.\nIndeed the watch of the night is firmer in tread and more upright in respect to speech,\nاِنَّ لَكَ فِى النَّهَارِ سَبْحًا طَوِيْلًا ؕ‏(7)\nINNAA LAKA FIN NAHAARE SABHAN TAWEELAA.\nfor indeed during the day you have drawn-out engagements.\nوَاذْكُرِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ وَتَبَتَّلْ اِلَيْهِ تَبْتِيْلًا ؕ‏(8)\nWAZ KORISMA RABBEKA WA TABATTAL ELAYHE TABTEELAA.\nSo celebrate the Name of your Lord and dedicate yourself to Him with total dedication.\nرَبُّ الْمَشْرِقِ وَالْمَغْرِبِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ فَاتَّخِذْهُ وَكِيْلًا‏(9)\nRABBUL MASHREQE WAL MAGHREBE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FAT-TAKHIZHO WAKEELAA.\nLord of the east and the west, there is no god except Him; so take Him for your trustee,\nوَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَاهْجُرْهُمْ هَجْرًا جَمِيْلًا‏(10)\nWAS BIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WAH JURHUM HAJRAN JAMEELAA.\nand be patient over what they say, and distance yourself from them in a graceful manner.\nوَذَرْنِىْ وَالْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ اُولِى النَّعْمَةِ وَمَهِّلْهُمْ قَلِيْلًا‏(11)\nWA ZARNEE WAL MOKAZZEBEENA OOLIN NA’MATE WA MAH-HILHUM QALEELAA.\nLeave Me [to deal] with the deniers, the opulent, and give them a little respite.\nاِنَّ لَدَيْنَاۤ اَنْكَالًا وَّجَحِيْمًا ۙ‏(12)\nINNA LADAYNAA ANKAALANW WA JAHEEMANW.\nIndeed with Us are heavy fetters and a fierce fire,\nوَّطَعَامًا ذَا غُصَّةٍ وَّعَذَابًا اَلِيْمًا‏(13)\nWA TA-A’AMAN ZAA GHUSSATINW WA A’ZAABAN ALEEMAA.\nand a food that chokes [those who eat it], and a painful punishment [prepared for]\nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الْاَرْضُ وَالْجِبَالُ وَكَانَتِ الْجِبَالُ كَثِيْبًا مَّهِيْلًا‏(14)\nYAWMA TARJOFUL ARZO WAL JEBAALO WA KAANATIL JEBAALO KASEEBAM MAHEELAA.\nthe day when the earth and the mountains will quake, and the mountains will be like dunes of shifting sand.\nاِنَّاۤ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ رَسُوْلًا ۙ شَاهِدًا عَلَيْكُمْ كَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ رَسُوْلًا ؕ‏(15)\nINNAA ARSALNAA ELAYKUM RASOOLAN, SHAA-HEDAN A’LAYKUM KAMAA ARSALNAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA RASOOLAA.\nIndeed We have sent to you an apostle, to be a witness to you, just as We sent an apostle to Pharaoh.\nفَعَصٰى فِرْعَوْنُ الرَّسُوْلَ فَاَخَذْنٰهُ اَخْذًا وَّبِيْلًا‏(16)\nFA-A’SAA FIR-A’WNUR RASOOLA FA-AKHAZNAAHO AKH-ZANW WABEELAA.\nBut Pharaoh disobeyed the apostle; so We seized him with a terrible seizing.\nفَكَيْفَ تَتَّقُوْنَ اِنْ كَفَرْتُمْ يَوْمًا يَّجْعَلُ الْوِلْدَانَ شِيْبَا  ۖ‏(17)\nFA-KAYFA TAT-TAQOONA IN KAFARTUM YAWMAY YAJ-A’LUL WILDAANA SHEE-BAA. NIS\nSo, if you disbelieve, how will you avoid the day, which will make children white-headed,\nاۨلسَّمَآءُ مُنْفَطِرٌ ۢ بِهٖؕ كَانَ وَعْدُهٗ مَفْعُوْلًا‏(18)\nSAMAAA-O MUNFATERUM BEH, KAANAA WA’DOHU MAF-O’OLAA.\nand wherein the sky will be rent apart? His promise is bound to be fulfilled.\nاِنَّ هٰذِهٖ تَذْكِرَةٌ  ۚ فَمَنْ شَآءَ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰى رَبِّهٖ سَبِيْلًا‏(19)\nINNA HAAZEHI TAZKERAH, FAMAN SHAAA-AT TAKHAZA ELAA RABBEHI SABEELAA.\nThis is indeed a reminder. So let anyone who wishes take the way toward his Lord.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَعْلَمُ اَنَّكَ تَقُوْمُ اَدْنىٰ مِنْ ثُلُثَىِ الَّيْلِ وَ نِصْفَهٗ وَثُلُثَهٗ وَطَآئِفَةٌ مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ مَعَكَؕ وَاللّٰهُ يُقَدِّرُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَؕ عَلِمَ اَنْ لَّنْ تُحْصُوْهُ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ فَاقْرَءُوْا مَا تَيَسَّرَ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِؕ عَلِمَ اَنْ سَيَكُوْنُ مِنْكُمْ مَّرْضٰىۙ وَاٰخَرُوْنَ يَضْرِبُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ يَبْتَغُوْنَ مِنْ فَضْلِ اللّٰهِۙ وَاٰخَرُوْنَ يُقَاتِلُوْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ۖ فَاقْرَءُوْا مَا تَيَسَّرَ مِنْهُ ۙ وَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَاٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَقْرِضُوا اللّٰهَ قَرْضًا حَسَنًا ؕ وَمَا تُقَدِّمُوْا لِاَنْفُسِكُمْ مِّنْ خَيْرٍ تَجِدُوْهُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ هُوَ خَيْرًا وَّاَعْظَمَ اَجْرًا ؕ وَاسْتَغْفِرُوا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(20)\nINNA RABBAKA YA’LAMO ANNAKA TAQOOMO ADNAA MIN SOLOSAYIL LAYLE WA NISFAHU WA SOLOSAHU WA TAAA-EFATUM MENAL LAZEENA MA-A’K, WAL LAAHO YOQADDERUL LAYLA WAN NAHAAR, A’LEMA AL LAN TOHSOOHO FA-TAABA A’LAYKUM FAQ-RA-OO MAA TAYASSARA MENAL QUR-AAN, A’LEMA AN SAYAKOONO MINKUM MARZAA, WA AAKHAROONA YAZREBOONA FIL ARZE YABTAGHOONA MIN FAZLIL LAAH, WA AAKHAROONA YOQAATELOONA FEE SABEELIL LAAH, FAQ-RA-OO MAA TAYASSARA MINHO, WA AQEEMOOS SALAATA WA AATUZ ZAKAATA WA AQREZUL LAAHA QARZAN HASANAA, WA MAA TOQADDEMOO LE-ANFOSEKUM MIN KHAYRIN TAJEDOOHO I’NDAL LAAHE HOWA KHAYRANW WA A-A’ZAMA AJRAA, WAS TAGHFERUL LAAH, INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord knows that you stand vigil for nearly two thirds of the night—or [at times] a half or a third of it—along with a group of those who are with you. Allah measures the night and the day. He knows that you cannot calculate it [exactly], and so He was lenient toward you. So recite as much of the Quran as is feasible. He knows that some of you will be sick, while others will travel in the land seeking Allah’s bounty, and yet others will fight in the way of Allah. So recite as much of it as is feasible, and maintain the prayer and pay the zakat and lend Allah a good loan. Whatever good you send ahead for your souls you will find it with Allah [in a form] that is better and greater with respect to reward. And plead to Allah for forgiveness; indeed Allah is all-forgiving, all-merciful.",
  "merits": "There are 20 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. Some scholars say that it was revealed in Madinah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that a person who recites this Surah will never face bad times. The person who recites it in the Isha or Tahajjud prayers always remains pure of heart and even dies while he is in a pure state.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) said that a person who recites this Surah properly will get a chance to meet the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and if he prays for something from Allah (s.w.t.) he will get it. Reciting Surah al-Muzammil a hundred times on Thursday night leads to the forgiving of a hundred major sins and procures a hundred rewards. Recitation of this Surah protects one from insanity and from being a slave to people."
